Fri Nov 20 09:40:04 1998  Martin Reddy  <reddy@Lomond.AI.SRI.COM>

	* acinclude.m4: Fixed the generation of the intxx_t and u_intxx_t
	defines. Previously these put a dollar symbol into the config
	file, such as "#define int32 $int32". These appears to be because
	the AC_CHECK_TYPE was taking $int32 as a literal string and not a
	variable. This problem only raises it's head on non-sgi platforms.

	* acconfig.h: added comment to describe the fixed bit-size defines

	* configure.in: added an AC_TRY_COMPILE check to see if the
 	compiler can handle static initialisations with stderr and
 	stdout. Under WinNT, because of the way the Nutcracker stdio.h
 	defines stdio and stderr, you cannot do this. configure will now
 	set the value of HAVE_STATIC_INIT accordingly in config.h.

	* report.c: if the compiler can perform static initialisations
 	with stderr then do it for trace_stream, otherwise we use #define
